-- ============================================================================
-- D5 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Applied AI and Language Models, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/appliedai/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: RETRIEVAL AND CITED ANSWERS, BY HAND. What a copilot
-- and a retrieval step do; the tokeniser, the stop list left off; TF-IDF with
-- the smoothed idf, unit vectors and the cosine; BM25 with the Lucene idf, k1
-- saturation, b length normalisation and a score read term by term; the
-- ranking and its twelve-digit tie rule; precision, recall, hit and
-- reciprocal rank at a cutoff and their means; answers that cite their
-- sources, and unsupported claims. Digest sections 1 to 10, and section 24.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A retrieval score matches words, and a cited
-- figure is checkable only in a passage the answer cites and retrieved. No
-- language model runs anywhere in this course and no graded value depends on
-- one. The Associate capstone grades six Associate quantities and grades no
-- MAP, no nDCG, no extraction and no kappa.
-- ============================================================================

values ('appliedai', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-copilots-and-retrieval-do","title":"What Copilots and Retrieval Do","lesson_keys":["l01-a-question-a-search-and-an-answer","l02-retrieval-before-the-answer","l03-the-ekene-document-set","l04-what-is-graded-and-what-never-is","l05-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-tokens","title":"Tokens","lesson_keys":["l01-lowercase-and-split","l02-numbers-and-well-names-split","l03-the-stop-list-left-off","l04-counting-terms"]},{"key":"m03-tf-idf","title":"TF-IDF","lesson_keys":["l01-term-and-document-frequency","l02-the-smoothed-idf","l03-unit-length-vectors","l04-cosine-ranking"]},{"key":"m04-bm25","title":"BM25","lesson_keys":["l01-the-bm25-idf","l02-saturation-and-k1","l03-length-normalisation-and-b","l04-a-repeated-query-word","l05-bm25-term-by-term"]},{"key":"m05-ranking-and-metrics-at-k","title":"Ranking and Metrics at a Cutoff","lesson_keys":["l01-score-order-and-ties","l02-precision-and-recall-at-k","l03-hit-and-reciprocal-rank","l04-means-over-queries"]},{"key":"m06-answers-that-cite-sources","title":"Answers That Cite Their Sources","lesson_keys":["l01-prompts-that-ask-for-citations","l02-claims-in-an-answer","l03-unsupported-claims","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
